uces** evidence before one **raises an objection**. **It is not the conclusion that persuades, but the care.**","**Not until** the argument has been **reconstructed** **do critics ask** whether it is sound. **Rarely does** a seminar end in agreement; **it is high time** we accepted that as **a virtue**. **Granted**, patience is slow, but it is **seldom wasted**."],"kicker":"REPORT","by":"Seminar Society","gloss":[["take for granted","dar como certo"],["rival","rival"],["virtue","virtude"],["seldom","raramente"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"The report says philosophers accept things for granted.","ans":"F","why":"take nothing for granted."},{"q":"The report says seminars rarely end in agreement.","ans":"T","why":"Rarely does a seminar end in agreement."},{"q":"The report claims patience is never wasted.","ans":"F","why":"seldom wasted."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“adduce” = ?","opts":["apresentar como prova","somar","deduzir"],"ans":0,"why":"adduce."},{"q":"“Rarely does…” introduces…","opts":["inversão","pergunta","imperativo"],"ans":0,"why":"negative adverb + auxiliary."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Grammar recap","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Verifique","Exemplo"],"rows":[["**Cautela epistêmica**","I would be **reluctant to say**…; **It seems to me**…"],["**convince × persuade**","**convinced that** × **persuaded to**"],["**Frases clivadas e inversão**","**What matters is**…; **Not until** X **does** Y"],["**Instruções e finalidade**","**in order to**; **so that**"],["**Editorial**","**It is high time** we **stopped**"]],"cap":"Lista de verificação da Unidade 9 (C2)"}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice · Mixed review","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences (from the unit)","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"Firms ___ to be able to explain how their systems decide. (ought)","a":"ought","why":"dever."},{"s":"This study ___ whether thou